Parallel precision regression tests
===================================

  timeout 180 ./maxima-local --no-init --lisp=sbcl \
    --batch-string='run_testsuite(tests=[rtest_parallel_precision,rtest_parallel_input,rtest_parallel_loop,rtest_parallel,rtest_ask1]);'

Run each configured Lisp and require "No unexpected errors" in the log.
A zero process status alone does not prove that Maxima had no Lisp errors.
The new file is included in the complete suite automatically.

The 17 examples cover five fixed decimal precisions, inherited working
precision, the four associated constants, error cleanup, the one-core
fallback, actual workers and nested parallel computations. The forced
worker helper comes from parallel-input-check.lisp, so inheritance does
not pass merely because the calling thread took every queued item.

Numerical assertions decode the stored bigfloat to an exact binary
rational, then compare it with an independent rational reference and a
relative error bound determined by the requested decimal precision.
They also compare all six precision-state values with the caller's
snapshot. A private deterministic LCG generates 64 further cases with
12 through 200 decimal digits and signed rational inputs. It does not
change Maxima's random state.

Temporary changes to the internal working bit precision are copied
unchanged; recomputing it from the public decimal precision would lose
valid caller state. Precision assignments made in an ordinary sequential
MAKELIST retain their existing behavior.
